**Change 1: highlight_match in commands_search.rs** — Fixes a real Unicode safety bug. The old code used `path_lower.rfind()` which returns byte offsets in the lowercased string, then used those offsets to slice the original string. When to_lowercase() changes byte length (e.g., Turkish İ → i̇), this causes byte-offset mismatches and potential panics. The new code uses char-level indexing with proper mapping back to original byte boundaries.

